    <md:uuid>3639fd0a-a849-4013-bbaf-7adc7006f040</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will write a system of equations from a table of values, graphs, and situations. You will also be able to graph systems by hand and use graphs of systems of equations to estimate real world solutions.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Write a system of equations from tables of values and graphs. </item>
  <item> Graph systems of equations by hand. </item>
  <item> Estimate real-world solutions by graphing systems of equations. </item>
</list>

<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 2.2.1: Interpreting Graphs of Systems of Equations </item>
  <item> 2.2.2: Writing Systems of Equations from Tables </item>
  <list>
    <item> 2.2.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 2.2.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 2.2.3: Graphs of Systems of Equations </item>
  <list>
    <item> 2.2.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 2.2.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 2.2.4: Systems of Equations in the Real-World </item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 2.2.5: Practice </item>
  <item> 2.2.6: Lesson Summary </item>
</list>
</section>
</content>
